### 5. TCP Video Streaming Experiment

Attempted live video streaming using libcamera.

Initial command:

```bash
rpicam-vid -t 0 --inline --listen -o tcp://0.0.0.0:8888
```

Issue:

```text
failed to bind listen socket
```

Diagnosis:

Existing process occupying specified port.

Resolution:

Terminate previous camera processes.

```bash
pkill -f rpicam-vid
```

Retry using alternate port:

```bash
rpicam-vid -t 0 --inline --listen -o tcp://0.0.0.0:9999
```

Outcome:

- Stream started correctly
- Further client-side testing required

Result:

✅ Stream server launching successfully

